        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging Vancouver, BC",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is a digital marketing technique for real estate photos: an interior designer adds 3D furniture and decor to empty or cleared rooms so potential buyers can see how the space lives, with no physical furniture ever entering the home. Bella is headquartered in Vancouver, and our designers stage Lower Mainland listings in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "Vancouver",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the Vancouver real estate market",
        "market_text": "<p>Vancouver buyers shop online first, and the region's housing stock is hard on empty photos: glass condo towers shot against grey skies read cold, and compact downtown floor plans look even smaller unfurnished. Home staging fills the square footage believably, so a 550 sq ft Yaletown one-bed reads as a home rather than a box with a view — helping buyers envision the space and building the emotional connection that gets a listing shortlisted.</p><p>The light is a genuine technical problem here for much of the year. An empty white-walled unit photographed under overcast Vancouver skies has almost no warmth in it, and no amount of exposure correction adds the furniture, texture and colour that make a room feel lived in. Staging makes property listings visually appealing without changing the room itself.</p><p>The rest of the Lower Mainland adds variety: townhomes and detached homes in Burnaby, Coquitlam and Surrey, family houses in Langley and the Fraser Valley, and new construction and presale inventory from developers across the region. Each of those buyers is looking for something different, and staging lets the photos show it.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Virtual staging Vancouver: condos, townhomes and detached homes",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage clean contemporary for Yaletown, Coal Harbour and downtown towers, West Coast warmth for Kitsilano, Mount Pleasant and East Van character homes, and family looks for Burnaby, Richmond, North Vancouver and the suburbs. Compact floor plans get furnished to scale rather than flattered: in a market this expensive per square foot, buyers measure carefully, and staging that oversells a room loses the trust it was meant to build.</p><p>Our team works online, so there is no consultation to schedule: order, upload your photos and your designer handles the interior design, furniture and accessories. Files come back MLS-ready for Realtor.ca in 24 to 48 hours with disclosure guidance. In BC, the BC Financial Services Authority says licensees should label photos that have been altered or enhanced, such as virtually staged photos, so they don't mislead a potential buyer — see our <a href=\"/pages/resources-mls-rules-canada\">Canadian virtual staging compliance guide</a>.</p><p>Volume discounts apply automatically: 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Yaletown, Coal Harbour, Kitsilano, Mount Pleasant, East Vancouver, West End, Burnaby, Richmond, North Vancouver, Surrey",
        "cred_text": ""
      }
