        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does home staging cost in Vancouver?",
            "answer": "Physical staging is priced by the stager, the size of the home and how long the furniture stays, so quotes vary; as a general benchmark, conventional staging runs about $2,000–5,000 a month until the home sells. Virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, paid once, with no rental period to extend."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging allowed in BC?",
            "answer": "Yes. The BC Financial Services Authority says it may be okay to virtually stage a house, but licensees should label photos that have been altered or enhanced so they don't mislead a potential buyer. Add furniture and decor only and never change the property's permanent features. Every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are you based in Vancouver?",
            "answer": "Yes — Bella is headquartered in Vancouver and stages listings for agents, developers and homeowners across BC, the rest of Canada and the US. Everything is ordered online, so it works the same for a Yaletown condo or a Langley detached home."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My photos were shot on a grey day and everything looks cold. Can you fix that?",
            "answer": "That's a large part of what staging does here. Furniture, texture and colour put warmth into a room that overcast light strips out — and where the exterior needs help, day-to-dusk editing is available too."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this AI staging?",
            "answer": "No. Every image is composed by hand by a professional interior designer. AI staging tends to invent details and repeat the same room across a market — on Vancouver price points, that's not a risk worth taking with a listing."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you stage presale and new construction units?",
            "answer": "Yes. Completed but empty units are staged from photos like any vacant home. For homes that aren't built yet, 3D rendering from your drawings is the better fit."
          }
        },
